        "A practical succession planning framework for small to mid-size organizations involves four disciplines practiced concurrently. First, talent identification: at every level, asking who are the one or two people with the highest potential to take on greater responsibility, and what would need to be true for them to be ready? Second, deliberate development: creating specific opportunities -- stretch assignments, cross-functional exposure, increased decision-making authority -- that develop identified people rather than merely expose them to more work. Third, knowledge transfer: systematically surfacing and passing on institutional knowledge, relationships, and judgment that currently lives only in the heads of experienced leaders. Fourth, cultural transmission: ensuring that the values, norms, and decision-making principles of the organization are embedded in structures, stories, and practices that outlast any individual leader.",
