        "Leadership bench depth is perhaps the single most important legacy indicator. An organization with a deep bench -- multiple people at each leadership level who are being actively developed and who are capable of stepping up -- is an organization that can absorb shocks, pursue opportunities, and sustain performance across leadership transitions. An organization with a thin bench is one disruption away from a talent crisis. Measuring bench depth requires a regular leadership talent review: who is ready for increased responsibility now, who will be ready in one to two years, and who has high potential that needs to be deliberately developed.",
